title: AURA: She Blooms — Seeing a Better Self in Intimate Relationships

time: Sunday, March 8, 2026 | 1:00 PM – 5:00 PM

address: 100 Galen St #204, Watertown, MA 02472

summary: 
Organized by the Asian American Wellness and Beauty Association (AAWBA), this International Women’s Day special event features an empowering salon lecture by Dr. Feng Li. Designed to foster personal growth, emotional connection, and self-awareness within intimate relationships, the afternoon combines an expert talk, interactive Q&A, guided relaxation meditation, and networking opportunities.

description:
About the Event
To celebrate International Women’s Day, AAWBA invites you to “AURA: She Blooms,” a transformative workshop centered on the theme: “Discovering a Better Version of Yourself in Intimate Relationships.” Learn how to express yourself with gentle firmness, build clear and powerful connections, and cultivate personal growth within your meaningful relationships.

Keynote Speaker: Dr. Feng Li
Ph.D. in Biomedical Sciences

Harvard Early Childhood Leadership Certificate

Family Growth Coach: Hands-on experience with over 50 families and 100+ deep case consultations.

Event Agenda
1:00 PM – 2:30 PM | Check-in & Light Refreshments

Complete check-in, collect event materials, and enjoy casual networking over light tea and snacks.

2:30 PM – 3:30 PM | Keynote Lecture with Dr. Feng Li

A systematic presentation covering emotional understanding, communication strategies, self-awareness, and personal growth in intimate relationships.

3:30 PM – 4:00 PM | Interactive Q&A Session

An open discussion addressing real-life relationship conflicts, root causes, and practical solutions for improvement.

4:00 PM – 4:30 PM | Guided Meditation & Relaxation

A relaxing session focused on releasing stress, calming the mind, and stabilizing your inner state.

4:30 PM – 5:00 PM | Event Wrap-Up & Group Photo

Review key takeaways, reflect on personal growth directions, and capture memories with a group photo session.